1
00:00:18,920 --> 00:00:22,777
When Sir Alex Ferguson took that
microphone in May 2013,

2
00:00:22,827 --> 00:00:26,318
he asked the people of Old
Trafford for one thing:

3
00:00:26,368 --> 00:00:28,577
to stand by the next manager,

4
00:00:28,627 --> 00:00:32,790
the same way the club had stood by
him through the bad years.

5
00:00:33,140 --> 00:00:35,831
Thirteen years and seven sackings later,

6
00:00:35,881 --> 00:00:39,029
Manchester United have just
unveiled the eighth,

7
00:00:39,079 --> 00:00:43,940
and the strange part is that no manager in
the world looks more like the young

8
00:00:43,990 --> 00:00:46,338
Ferguson than Mauricio Pochettino.

9
00:00:46,688 --> 00:00:49,683
Both walked into clubs
sinking down the table,

10
00:00:49,733 --> 00:00:52,841
both bet everything on kids
nobody had heard of,

11
00:00:52,891 --> 00:00:55,830
and both went years without
lifting a trophy.

12
00:00:56,180 --> 00:00:59,512
The difference is that United
waited for Ferguson.

13
00:00:59,562 --> 00:01:03,127
This video asks whether they
will wait for Pochettino,

14
00:01:03,177 --> 00:01:06,042
because his very first game is at Anfield.

15
00:01:10,992 --> 00:01:12,285
Before we start,

16
00:01:12,335 --> 00:01:16,202
if you also think United's problem
was never just the manager,

17
00:01:16,252 --> 00:01:17,937
hit like and subscribe,

18
00:01:17,987 --> 00:01:22,750
and send this to that one United fan who
swears that this time it's different.

19
00:01:23,100 --> 00:01:24,593
In November 1986,

20
00:01:24,643 --> 00:01:27,310
when Ferguson arrived from Aberdeen,

21
00:01:27,360 --> 00:01:31,631
Manchester United were twenty-first
in a league of twenty-two,

22
00:01:31,681 --> 00:01:35,026
looking straight down at the
relegation places.

23
00:01:35,376 --> 00:01:37,213
He changed the discipline,

24
00:01:37,263 --> 00:01:39,267
the training and the academy,

25
00:01:39,317 --> 00:01:43,153
and still went more than three years
without winning anything,

26
00:01:43,203 --> 00:01:45,596
until a banner at Old Trafford read:

27
00:01:45,646 --> 00:01:48,094
three years of excuses, ta-ra Fergie.

28
00:01:48,444 --> 00:01:50,671
The club did not sack him,

29
00:01:50,721 --> 00:01:55,762
and in May 1990 came the FA Cup, the
first of thirty-eight trophies.

30
00:01:56,112 --> 00:01:58,039
Twenty-three years later,

31
00:01:58,089 --> 00:01:59,476
in January 2009,

32
00:01:59,526 --> 00:02:01,872
a thirty-six-year-old Argentine,

33
00:02:01,922 --> 00:02:06,964
whose only coaching experience was a few
months with Espanyol's women's team,

34
00:02:07,014 --> 00:02:10,318
took over the first team in
the relegation zone.

35
00:02:10,668 --> 00:02:15,823
Within a month he walked into the Camp Nou
with the bottom side in Spain and beat

36
00:02:15,873 --> 00:02:17,578
Guardiola's Barcelona,

37
00:02:17,628 --> 00:02:20,795
the team that would win
everything that season.

38
00:02:20,845 --> 00:02:24,538
It was Espanyol's first win there
in twenty-seven years.

39
00:02:24,888 --> 00:02:26,239
He had no money,

40
00:02:26,289 --> 00:02:29,099
so he did exactly what Ferguson had done:

41
00:02:29,149 --> 00:02:33,886
he opened the academy door and gave debuts
to more than a dozen teenagers.

42
00:02:34,236 --> 00:02:35,277
In England,

43
00:02:35,327 --> 00:02:37,803
the resemblance became even clearer.

44
00:02:37,853 --> 00:02:42,912
At Southampton he turned a newly promoted
side into a pressing machine and gave a

45
00:02:42,962 --> 00:02:46,988
seventeen-year-old left-back called
Luke Shaw his breakthrough,

46
00:02:47,038 --> 00:02:49,858
before Shaw was sold to Manchester United.

47
00:02:50,208 --> 00:02:54,809
At Tottenham he made a
twenty-one-year-old Harry Kane his number nine,

48
00:02:54,859 --> 00:02:58,922
signed Dele Alli from MK Dons for
around five million pounds,

49
00:02:58,972 --> 00:03:04,348
and five seasons later took Spurs to the first
Champions League final in the club's

50
00:03:04,398 --> 00:03:05,302
history.

51
00:03:05,652 --> 00:03:08,260
But this is where the two stories split.

52
00:03:08,310 --> 00:03:11,362
Ferguson was given time to
win his first trophy,

53
00:03:11,412 --> 00:03:14,574
and Pochettino has still never
won one in England.

54
00:03:14,624 --> 00:03:16,624
Five months after that final,

55
00:03:16,674 --> 00:03:19,282
he was sacked with Tottenham fourteenth.

56
00:03:19,632 --> 00:03:24,381
At PSG he won trophies with a team of
superstars who would not press,

57
00:03:24,431 --> 00:03:27,496
the opposite of everything he believes in,

58
00:03:27,546 --> 00:03:30,550
and at Chelsea he lasted a single season.

59
00:03:30,900 --> 00:03:32,406
And all that time,

60
00:03:32,456 --> 00:03:34,201
Ferguson was watching.

61
00:03:34,251 --> 00:03:35,159
In 2016,

62
00:03:35,209 --> 00:03:38,929
the manager Ferguson wanted at
Old Trafford had a name.

63
00:03:38,979 --> 00:03:40,964
United chose someone else,

64
00:03:41,014 --> 00:03:44,794
and it was not the first time the
club ignored Ferguson.

65
00:03:45,144 --> 00:03:46,438
Three years earlier,

66
00:03:46,488 --> 00:03:48,358
he had picked his own successor,

67
00:03:48,408 --> 00:03:50,854
and that choice lasted less
than ten months.

68
00:03:51,204 --> 00:03:54,060
David Moyes arrived as The Chosen One,

69
00:03:54,110 --> 00:03:57,535
with a banner on the
Stretford End to prove it,

70
00:03:57,585 --> 00:03:59,178
and in April 2014,

71
00:03:59,228 --> 00:04:02,842
after losing at his old club
Everton, he was gone.

72
00:04:03,192 --> 00:04:07,408
So United stopped trying to copy
Ferguson and hired his opposite,

73
00:04:07,458 --> 00:04:08,752
Louis van Gaal,

74
00:04:08,802 --> 00:04:11,908
a Dutchman of spreadsheets
and rigid patterns,

75
00:04:11,958 --> 00:04:16,174
whose football was so slow that Old
Trafford started to complain.

76
00:04:16,524 --> 00:04:18,924
He still won the FA Cup in 2016,

77
00:04:18,974 --> 00:04:22,108
and two days after that
final he was sacked,

78
00:04:22,158 --> 00:04:27,130
with reports of his replacement breaking
on the night of the final itself.

79
00:04:27,480 --> 00:04:30,177
Then came the manager the
whole world knew,

80
00:04:30,227 --> 00:04:31,361
José Mourinho.

81
00:04:31,411 --> 00:04:35,239
He won the League Cup and the Europa
League in his first season,

82
00:04:35,289 --> 00:04:37,178
finished second in the next,

83
00:04:37,228 --> 00:04:40,948
and then said a sentence that
sounded like a joke at the time,

84
00:04:40,998 --> 00:04:43,102
and sounds very different today.

85
00:04:55,852 --> 00:04:58,915
Less than four months later
he was gone too,

86
00:04:58,965 --> 00:05:03,585
so the club bet on nostalgia and called
one of Ferguson's own players,

87
00:05:03,635 --> 00:05:05,261
Ole Gunnar Solskjær,

88
00:05:05,311 --> 00:05:08,195
who started by winning almost everything,

89
00:05:08,245 --> 00:05:12,146
knocked PSG out in Paris and
became a hero all over again.

90
00:05:12,496 --> 00:05:16,915
But a team built on emotion does
not survive three seasons,

91
00:05:16,965 --> 00:05:18,849
and in November 2021,

92
00:05:18,899 --> 00:05:22,718
after losing four-one at
Watford, he left as well.

93
00:05:23,068 --> 00:05:26,579
The man brought in to fix the
house was Ralf Rangnick,

94
00:05:26,629 --> 00:05:29,910
the man who shaped half of
modern German football,

95
00:05:29,960 --> 00:05:34,850
and it did not take him long to say in
public what nobody inside dared to say.

96
00:05:44,100 --> 00:05:45,848
Keep that sentence in mind,

97
00:05:45,898 --> 00:05:48,672
because it comes back at the
end of this video.

98
00:05:48,722 --> 00:05:49,700
And quickly,

99
00:05:49,750 --> 00:05:51,343
tell me in the comments:

100
00:05:51,393 --> 00:05:52,730
of all these names,

101
00:05:52,780 --> 00:05:55,195
which United manager deserved more time?

102
00:05:55,245 --> 00:05:56,890
I'm reading every answer.

103
00:05:57,240 --> 00:06:00,599
Look at the queue closely and
something strange appears,

104
00:06:00,649 --> 00:06:04,062
because United do not sack their
managers when they fail.

105
00:06:04,112 --> 00:06:06,406
They sack them right after they win.

106
00:06:06,756 --> 00:06:10,582
Van Gaal won a cup and was
gone two days later.

107
00:06:10,632 --> 00:06:13,965
Erik ten Hag won the League Cup in 2023,

108
00:06:14,015 --> 00:06:17,065
beat City to win the FA Cup in 2024,

109
00:06:17,115 --> 00:06:22,210
was handed a new contract that
summer, and was sacked in October.

110
00:06:22,560 --> 00:06:26,218
Rúben Amorim arrived promising
a project of years,

111
00:06:26,268 --> 00:06:29,543
took the team to a European
final in Bilbao,

112
00:06:29,593 --> 00:06:31,397
lost it to Tottenham,

113
00:06:31,447 --> 00:06:34,274
and finished fifteenth in the league,

114
00:06:34,324 --> 00:06:37,918
the club's worst season since
relegation in 1974.

115
00:06:38,268 --> 00:06:39,662
In January this year,

116
00:06:39,712 --> 00:06:41,504
the day before he was sacked,

117
00:06:41,554 --> 00:06:44,242
he said the sentence that
explained everything.

118
00:06:58,392 --> 00:07:01,097
And then came the cruellest story of all.

119
00:07:01,147 --> 00:07:02,447
Michael Carrick,

120
00:07:02,497 --> 00:07:04,809
another son of the Ferguson years,

121
00:07:04,859 --> 00:07:07,058
took over as interim in January,

122
00:07:07,108 --> 00:07:09,307
won eleven of his sixteen games,

123
00:07:09,357 --> 00:07:12,006
put United back in the Champions League,

124
00:07:12,056 --> 00:07:15,886
and was given the job permanently
in May, on a two-year deal.

125
00:07:16,236 --> 00:07:17,553
Six months later,

126
00:07:17,603 --> 00:07:21,763
with one win in ten league games and
the team in the relegation zone,

127
00:07:21,813 --> 00:07:22,966
he was sacked.

128
00:07:23,016 --> 00:07:26,958
For the first time in a hundred and
forty-eight years of history,

129
00:07:27,008 --> 00:07:31,114
Manchester United had sacked two
managers in the same calendar year.

130
00:07:31,464 --> 00:07:36,381
And the detail that hurts the most is who
climbed back to the top in the meantime:

131
00:07:36,431 --> 00:07:39,526
the very club Ferguson had
knocked off its perch.

132
00:07:39,876 --> 00:07:40,940
Liverpool,

133
00:07:40,990 --> 00:07:44,466
who in 2013 looked condemned
to live on memories,

134
00:07:44,516 --> 00:07:46,446
hired a manager in 2015,

135
00:07:46,496 --> 00:07:47,745
Jürgen Klopp,

136
00:07:47,795 --> 00:07:49,292
and let him work.

137
00:07:49,342 --> 00:07:54,922
It took four years to win the Champions
League, and five to win the Premier League.

138
00:07:55,272 --> 00:07:56,556
When Klopp left,

139
00:07:56,606 --> 00:07:59,558
the structure was so solid
that his successor,

140
00:07:59,608 --> 00:08:00,558
Arne Slot,

141
00:08:00,608 --> 00:08:03,171
won the title in his very first season,

142
00:08:03,221 --> 00:08:07,006
taking Liverpool to twenty English
titles, level with United.

143
00:08:07,356 --> 00:08:10,900
Everything Ferguson spent a
quarter of a century building,

144
00:08:10,950 --> 00:08:14,059
their rival won back in little
more than a decade,

145
00:08:14,109 --> 00:08:18,089
and they did it by doing exactly what
he asked for in that speech:

146
00:08:18,139 --> 00:08:20,050
they stood by their manager.

147
00:08:20,400 --> 00:08:25,193
This is the club Mauricio
Pochettino walks into now.

148
00:08:25,243 --> 00:08:27,857
His name came up in 2016,

149
00:08:27,907 --> 00:08:29,633
again in 2018,

150
00:08:29,683 --> 00:08:31,408
again in 2021,

151
00:08:31,458 --> 00:08:38,350
and in 2022 he was one of the last two
candidates before United chose Ten Hag.

152
00:08:38,700 --> 00:08:41,439
Ten years after Ferguson first wanted him,

153
00:08:41,489 --> 00:08:43,391
the club finally hires him,

154
00:08:43,441 --> 00:08:46,794
but not the Pochettino of the
Champions League final.

155
00:08:46,844 --> 00:08:51,033
They hire the one who has to drag a
team out of the relegation zone,

156
00:08:51,083 --> 00:08:54,826
with barely a week of training
before he walks into Anfield.

157
00:08:55,176 --> 00:08:58,280
Ferguson had three and a half
years without a trophy.

158
00:08:58,330 --> 00:09:00,814
Pochettino may not even get three months.

159
00:09:01,164 --> 00:09:05,422
Rangnick said in 2022 that this club
needed open-heart surgery,

160
00:09:05,472 --> 00:09:08,637
and that no single manager
could do it alone.

161
00:09:08,687 --> 00:09:12,459
Three permanent managers have
come and gone since then,

162
00:09:12,509 --> 00:09:15,250
and the patient is still on the table.

163
00:09:15,600 --> 00:09:17,349
So leave your answer below,

164
00:09:17,399 --> 00:09:18,583
no overthinking:

165
00:09:18,633 --> 00:09:21,513
does Pochettino make it to
the end of the season?

166
00:09:21,563 --> 00:09:22,438
Yes or no?

167
00:09:22,788 --> 00:09:24,222
Thirteen years ago,

168
00:09:24,272 --> 00:09:29,115
a seventy-one-year-old man stood in the
middle of the pitch and asked the fans to

169
00:09:29,165 --> 00:09:30,985
stand by the next manager,

170
00:09:31,035 --> 00:09:35,218
because he knew that no club wins by
changing direction every season.

171
00:09:35,568 --> 00:09:37,002
The fans did their part.

172
00:09:37,052 --> 00:09:38,254
The club never did.

173
00:09:38,604 --> 00:09:39,832
This Saturday,

174
00:09:39,882 --> 00:09:43,376
the eighth manager since
Ferguson walks into Anfield,

175
00:09:43,426 --> 00:09:46,979
the stadium Ferguson spent his
life trying to silence.

176
00:09:47,029 --> 00:09:51,743
And maybe the ghost haunting Manchester
United was never Ferguson himself.

177
00:09:51,793 --> 00:09:54,416
Maybe it is the advice he left behind,

178
00:09:54,466 --> 00:09:58,018
the one nobody inside that club
was willing to follow.
